s.  The park is a 1607 acre recreational facility located at the mouth of the Huron River on Lake Erie and consists of meadows, a marsh and lagoons.  It has a three-mile (5 km) shoreline along the lake and is a popular bird-watching site.  The Park has a wave action swimming pool, an 18-hole regulation golf course, the Marshlands Museum and Nature Center, boat launches and a marina.  The children's play area, previously featuring a child-size town, is now under construction as a newer, more modern, playscape area is being built.]\n\nQuestion: what is the 3112 acre Pennsylvania state park that took over 11,000 to make due to the wave action of lake Erie called?","terminal_format_issue":"Format Agent is not selected as the Output Agent","topology_statistics":{"agent_count":0,"component_count":0,"directed_edge_count":0,"fan_in_agent_ids":[],"fan_out_agent_ids":[],"max_depth":0,"max_width":0,"output_agent_id":null,"quotient_directed_edge_count":0,"reciprocal_pair_count":0,"relation_count":0,"root_agent_ids":[],"root_component_count":0,"sink_agent_ids":[],"sink_component_count":0,"structural_depth":0,"topology_family":"empty","topology_motifs":[]}}","role":"user"},{"content":"{"action":"add_agent","agent_id":"retrier","model_id":"qwen3.5-9b-local","contract":"Scan the provided passages to identify the Pennsylvania state park with 3112 acres and a 11,000-year history of formation via Lake Erie wave action; output the park's name.","role_family":"evidence"}","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Canvas observation. Choose exactly one next action using only the task, messages, Canvas, catalog, and any supplied validated Skill facts.

